            0.531,
            0.231,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "Also,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.564,
            0.789,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": "1 gram = 1000 milligrams (mg). So, 1 $mg = \\frac{1}{1000}   g  = 0.001   g .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.621,
            0.465,
            0.644
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Rupee ─ Paise conversion"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.652,
            0.849,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "You may have heard of ‘paisa’. 100 paise is equal to 1 rupee. As we have coins and notes for rupees, coins for paise were also used commonly until recently. There were coins for 1 paisa, 2 paise, 3 paise, 5 paise, 10 paise, 20 paise, 25 paise, and 50 paise. All denominations of 25 paise and less were removed from use in the year 2011. But we still see paise in bills, account statements, etc."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.4,
            0.768,
            0.599,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "1 { \\mathrm { ~ r u p e e } } = 1 0 0 { \\mathrm { ~ p a i s e } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.337,
            0.796,
            0.661,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "1\\  pairs =\\frac{1}{100}\\  type =0.01\\  type .",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.038,
            0.837,
            0.123,
            0.903
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
